\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuelan bolivar eases again to 504.50/505.50. \b0\par\par\uc2 127 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The Venezuelan bolivar eased by 25 centimes on Wednesday to close at 504.50/505.50 to the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggled to cover strong demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There was strong interbank demand, and to a lesser extent corporate buying, but the market was left short as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the last minute," said one. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is unusual in that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is usually its largest single supplier of dollars, which blurs the difference between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplying liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((-- Yelitza Cova, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2603, fax 582 861 3621, caracas.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du17017xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
