\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  bolivar ends firm on CenBnk  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, Aug 28 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed the Venezuelan bolivar Friday to a 495.50/496.50 per dollar close in a busy session marked by strong dollar demand, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The unit closed Thursday at 496/497 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Bank's forceful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been part of a wider strategy to drain excess bolivar liquidity from the financial system and maintain a strong bolivar as part of its anti-inflation fight. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is semi-anchoring the exchange rate to beat inflation," added one trader. \par \par \uc2  The Bank is due to release August's inflation figure on Monday and the rate is expected to top three percent. \par \par \uc2  Venezuela continues to pursue an inflation-fighting strong bolivar policy, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ostensibly floats between slowly depreciating bands set by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Critics say the policy has left the bolivar increasingly over-valued with the exchange rate little-changed since price and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls were removed in April last year. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8t00kpb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
