\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Closes Up Due To Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1997\par 23:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market drove the bolivar higher Friday, allowing it to make up a bit of the ground it lost in recent days, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at a midrate of 496.00 bolivars, down from Thursday's close of 497.00 bolivars. \par \par \uc2  The average bank spread was 495.50/496.50. Spreads of major banks ranged from 495.30/496.30 to 496.00/497.00. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold major sums of dollars throughout the day to bring support to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been sliding in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold between $80 million to $100 million in the course of the day. \par \par \uc2  'It sold dollars consistently throughout the day,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which by law must buy most of the dollars earned by state-run oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela S.A. (PdVSA), is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  Strong demand for dollars from corporations and other investors persisted Friday. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar's slide in recent weeks has made investors nervous this week that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to weaken, and they have consequently been buying up dollars as a hedge. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to drive the dollar down to 496.00 bolivars, corporations began buying up even more dollars as they figured they had to take advantage of the cheap price, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Going into Thursday's session, the bolivar had lost 1.7% over the previous 13 sessions. Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday kept the bolivar stable ahead of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -aided strengthening. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-08-97 \par \par \uc2  2143GMT \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8105n1o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
