\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Stronger On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1997\par 18:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (AP-Dow Jones)--Aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela brought support to the bolivar and drove it stronger against the dollar at midday Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at midday at a midrate of 496.00 bolivars, down from Thursday's close of 497.00. \par \par \uc2  The average bank spread was 495.50/496.50 bolivars. Spreads of major banks ranged from 495.50/496.50 to 496.00/497.00. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dumped dollars in the market throughout the course of the morning. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold at least $50 million and perhaps as much as $100 million. \par \par \uc2  Normally, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $15 million to $20 million in the mornings. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which by law must buy nearly all of the dollars earned by state-run oil company Petroleos de Venezuela S.A. (PdVSA), is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't just trying to meet dollar demand, but was looking to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Another trader agreed, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  inched down its dollar selling price from 497.25 bolivars to 495.75 bolivars during its rounds of dollar-selling this morning. \par \par \uc2  When the dollar began to weaken, corporations started snapping up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , taking advantage of the attractive price, trader said. \par \par \uc2  Because of the dollar has steadily strengthened against the bolivar in recent weeks, dollar demand has consequently risen as corporations and investors have hedged against a possible further weakening of the boliver. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, a slight rise in social tension has also caused nervous investors to increase their dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Tension has risen due to an increase in state-set gasoline prices on Thursday and the reluctance of businesses to grant wage rises promised during labor law reform talks earlier this year. \par \par \uc2  Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has allowed the bolivar to weaken in recent weeks - down 1.7% against the dollar between July 11 and July 31 - it appears to be now willing to move against any further sharp weakening in the short term in a bid to calm a nervous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1630GMT \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8105m91\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
