\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Closes Weaker;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 1997\par 23:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (AP-Dow Jones)--The bolivar closed weaker against the dollar Wednesday despite strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at a midrate of 497.00 bolivars, up from Tuesday's close of 496.50 bolivars. \par \par \uc2  The average bank spread was 496.50/497.50. Spreads of major banks ranged from 496.50/497.50 to 497.00/497.50. \par \par \uc2  Continuing social tension in Caracas kept corporations, banks and other investors nervous Wednesday, and this had them hedging their positions by moving money into dollars. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market aggressively selling dollars throughout the day to take pressure of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders estimated that it sold around $75 million. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which by law must buy most of the dollars earned by state-run oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela S.A. (PdVSA), is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar's slide Wednesday makes for the sixth straight session it has weakened. It has now fallen 1.7% since July 11, when it closed at 488.75 bolivars per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Venezuelan Workers Confederation (CTV), the nation's biggest labor union, called a nationwide 12-hour work stoppage for next Wednesday in an effort to coerce the business sector into granting workers the wage rises they agreed to in recent negotiations. \par \par \uc2  There is also a bit of unrest in the country ahead of Thursday's 27% increase in state-set domestic gasoline prices. \par \par \uc2  'This is definitely not a great moment for neither the stock exchange nor the bolivar due to the tension in the country,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the ratcheting higher of yields on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  TEM bills, the local interest rate bellwether, in Wednesday's primary auction did little to bring support to the bolivar. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the benchmark 178-day TEM bills rose 0.47 percentage point to 21.40%. \par \par \uc2  'The TEM yield rise had no impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for two reasons -- one because the rise wasn't that significant, and two because the market had already discounted the news for the most part,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-07-97 \par \par \uc2  2101GMT \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7u05o5x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
