\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela bolivar ends weaker at 492.50/493.50/dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, July 17 (Reuter) - The Venezuelan bolivar closed weaker at 492.50/493.50 per dollar Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars heavily to prevent a steeper slide of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar closed at 492.00/493.00 Wednesday and has slipped 4.25 bolivars per dollar so far this week. \par \par \uc2  "The market was heavily demanded, particularly on the corporate side and the dollar reached 494.50 bolivars. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in strongly and brought it down," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the heavy dollar demand was due largely to excess liquidity on money markets, echoing comments made by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Antonio Casas Gonzalez earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  They added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong dollar selling in the afternoon should calm market expectations that it was prepared to allow the bolivar to plummet further. \par \par \uc2  Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is unusual in that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is its largest single supplier of dollars, which blurs the difference between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplying liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to pursue an inflation-fighting strong bolivar policy, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ostensibly floats between slowly depreciating bands set by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Critics say the policy has left the bolivar increasingly over-valued with the exchange rate little-changed since price and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls were removed in April last year. \par \par \uc2  ((--Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7h02fjk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
