\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela bolivar ends softer at 489.25/490.25/dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, July 14 (Reuter) - The Venezuelan bolivar closed weaker at 489.25/490.25 per dollar Monday as an increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve requirement had little effect on market liquidity, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar closed at 488.25/489.25 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that banks had turned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after a new measure to raise the reserve requirement at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 12 to 15 percent had little effect on market liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "The effect of the new reserve requirement was not as expected and money markets remained liquid," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank overnight lending rates opened at 10 percent but later fell to about five percent, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Banks which sold dollars to meet the new reserve requirement in the morning "had to buy back their positions because the market remained very liquid," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the reserve requirement last week to tackle an expected bubble of excess liquidity in coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is unusual in that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is its largest single supplier of dollars, which blurs the difference between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplying liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to pursue an inflation-fighting strong bolivar policy, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ostensibly floats between slowly depreciating bands set by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Critics say the policy has left the bolivar increasingly over-valued with the exchange rate little-changed since price and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls were removed in April last year. \par \par \uc2  ((--Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02qca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
