\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela Bolivar Closes Weaker; Central Bk Unloads Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 22:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (AP-Dow Jones)--The bolivar closed weaker against the dollar Friday as heavy demand arose for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at a midrate of 484.25 bolivars, up from Thursday's close of 484.00 bolivars. \par \par \uc2  The average bank spread was 483.75/484.75. Spreads of major banks ranged from 483.00/484.25 to 484.00/484.85. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar, which has been gradually depreciating in recent weeks, weakened slightly Friday even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, selling dollars. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold anywhere from $60 million to $100 million during the course of the day. \par \par \uc2  'The bank unloaded a lot of dollars. It's that there was a lot of demand out there,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which by law must buy most of the dollars earned by state-run oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela SA (PdVSA), is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the strong demand for dollars was in part a continuation of the uptick in dollar buying by companies looking to import goods. A slowly-recovering economy, bouyed in part by recent wage rises in the public and private sectors, is increasing the country's import bill. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, dollar buying by foreign portfolio investors has also increased as they have been taking their money out of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  TEM bills and other local debt paper and moving it out of the country. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to let the bolivar slide gradually against the dollar in recent weeks has gotten the attention of foreign portfolio investors, traders said. \par \par \uc2  While a return in bolivars of roughly 18.00% on six-month TEM bills is attractive when depreciation expectations are minimal, it isn't attractive if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to allow the bolivar to slide as it has in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar has depreciated 1.5% since Apr. 3. \par \par \uc2  'Foreign investors in TEMs have been watching the bolivar's slide carefully, and some of them are taking their money out of the country,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  2053GMT \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03kdk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
