\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela bolivar ends flat on CenBnk dlr sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, May 16 (Reuter) - The Venezuelan bolivar closed flat at 483.25/484.25 per dollar as strong seasonal demand for dollars to finance imports was met by ample \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sales, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "This is a traditional time for imports, for replenishing inventories and buying primary goods," said one trader. "Demand for dollars was strong, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplied what was necessary." \par \par \uc2  Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is unusual in that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is its largest single supplier of dollars, which blurs the difference between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplying liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to pursue an inflation-fighting strong bolivar policy, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ostensibly floats between slowly depreciating bands set by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders say the Bank has recently relaxed its strong bolivar policy, letting the unit gently slide before it brushes against the lower band, last re-set in December. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5g05hbz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
