\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela bolivar ends soft as CenBnk stays away. \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, May 9 (Reuter) - The Venezuelan bolivar closed softer at 482.00/483.00 per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hung back from selling dollars into the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The unit closed Thursday at 481.50/482.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The bolivar fell as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold only few dollars into a moderately demanded market," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The Bank "wants to see the bolivar depreciate," he said, adding that the softer bolivar was also a likely result of the fall in interest rates at Wednesday's TEM bill auction. \par \par \uc2  Yields on benchmark six month TEM paper fell 123 basis points to 17.48 percent. \par \par \uc2  Other traders disagreed, however, saying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had in fact supplied most the market's dollar needs. \par \par \uc2  Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is unusual in that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is its largest single supplier of dollars, which blurs the difference between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplying liquidity and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to pursue an inflation-fighting strong bolivar policy, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ostensibly floats between slowly depreciating bands set by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Critics say the policy has left the bolivar increasingly over-valued with the exchange rate little-changed since price and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls were removed in April last year. \par \par \uc2  At current bolivar levels, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hit the bottom band by July. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5905v7b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
