\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  may tweak monetary policy. \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, April 17 (Reuter) - Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may tweak its monetary policy in light of higher government spending forecast for the year, but will hang tight with its current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director said. \par \par \uc2  Exchange rate policy will continue to "promote a fall in inflation while also allowing a reasonable degree of flexibility that avoids market distortions and negative effects," Bank director Carlos Hernandez Delfino told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Venezuelan inflation has steadily fallen since prices and exchange rate controls were liberalized last April -- but at the expense of an increasingly overvalued bolivar. \par \par \uc2  Although the bolivar floats freely between gently depreciating bands, its has only slipped some three percent against the dollar in the past year -- even as inflation has topped 70 percent. \par \par \uc2  Reducing inflation further -- March's 1.6 monthly rate was the lowest in five year -- remains a high government priority. Yet official inflation targets for the year have been upped to 35 percent, largely after a 70 percent public sector wage increase was agreed in February. \par \par \uc2  Hernandez said monetary policy would be determined by the state of Venezuelan fiscal accounts -- seen deteriorating from last year's one percent central government surplus due to the wage hike. \par \par \uc2  "Changes in these (fiscal) accounts will lead to some adjustments in the Bank's approach to monetary policy," Hernandez said. He details, except that the changes "are still being studied." \par \par \uc2  "Reducing inflation requires a high degree of financial, fiscal and monetary discipline, which also requires a high degree of institutional coordination between the Finance Ministry, PdVSA and the Bank," he added. \par \par \uc2  PdVSA is \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's state-owned oil industry. \par \par \uc2  Other than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary tools are currently limited to open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Bank-backed paper, called TEMs, in weekly auctions. Primarily used to soak-up excess liquidity, the TEMs are also taken as benchmark for wider interest rates. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4h06yyt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
