\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -3: To Sell Daily Quota,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 00:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In order to separate its role as 'supplier' of PdVSA dollars to the market and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  role in the market, the bank has decided to sell a quota of dollars each day that will constitute its dollar sales as a 'supplier,' the source said. \par \par \uc2  The source didn't say what that daily quota is. \par \par \uc2  Any subsequent dollar sales or purchases made in the day are to be deemed as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, the source said. \par \par \uc2  By selling its normal quota of dollars in the morning, the bank is letting the market set the exchange rate within levels that the bank can tolerate. \par \par \uc2  The bank's bands on the bolivar are 7.5% above and below the central parity, but the source indicated that the bank will often look to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market well before it gets close to the upper or lower levels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source indicated that greater volatility in the market will make foreign investors less eager to enter the local financial markets because they won't be able to easily forecast what rate they can pull their money out of the country. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seeking for ways to keep hot money, which has made a very strong bolivar even stronger, out of the country, bank officials have told Dow Jones Newswires. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Antonio Casas wouldn't respond when asked if the bank had implemented this mechanism of separating its roles as 'supplier' and '\b \highlight22\uc2 intervener\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' in the market. \par \par \uc2  'I can't talk about the technical workings of our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy,' he told Dow Jones Newswires in a telephone interview. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-03-97 \par \par \uc2  2337GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3301i8p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
