\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela Bolivar Closes Stronger As Ctrl Bank Sells Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 1996\par 22:30\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (Dow Jones)--The bolivar closed slightly stronger Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again aggresively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market selling dollars to protect the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 471.125 bolivars, down from Wednesday's close of 471.375 bolivars. \par \par \uc2  The bank spread was 470.5/471.75. Spreads from major banks ranged from 470/471 to 471/472.25. \par \par \uc2  For the second day in a row, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forcefully moved into the market to defend the bolivar, which has been under heavy pressure in recent days due to the strong fall in local interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold, and sold, and sold in the afternoon," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the bank sold between $30 million and $40 million Thursday, matching Wednesday's estimated figure. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only lightly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday morning, allowing the bolivar to slip to 472.625 bolivars to the dollar at midday. \par \par \uc2  On top of the local interest rate drop, traders said that May's high inflation rate of 12.6% and a similarly expected high rate in June are also putting pressure on the bolivar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite May's high inflation rate, the exchange rate has remained\par essentially stable since late April, making dollars more attractive.\par    -David Papadopoulos\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 06-06-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1630EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds6600cfs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
