\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela Bolivar Stronger As  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sells Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1996\par 22:44\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market aggressively Wednesday to protect a sagging bolivar and managed to strengthen the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at a midrate of 471.375 bolivars, down from Tuesday's close of 472 bolivars. \par \par \uc2  The bank spread was 470.75/472. Spreads from major banks ranged from 470.5/471.5 to 471.5/472.75. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that there was heavy corporate demand for dollars all day. That demand intensified, they said, when yields on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekly TEM bill auction came out in the afternoon down several percentage points from last week's yields. \par \par \uc2  Yields on TEM bills, which are the interest rate benchmark here, have crashed over the last several weeks. \par \par \uc2  "There were people taking positions in dollars (Wednesday) due to the TEM rate drop. And for the first time since this market has been opened up, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aggressively selling dollars to meet this demand," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Free \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading started up on April 22 after nearly two years of a rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  control system. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold between $30 million and $40 million Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its daily activities in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said that the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will most likely remain under\par pressure Thursday, and this will probably prompt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par stay in the market selling dollars.\par    -David Papadopoulos\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 06-05-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1644EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds6500ccb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
