\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2 's Bolivar Gains Vs Dlr;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 1996\par 23:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (AP-Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during afternoon trading Thursday to bolster the bolivar, but late demand for dollars after the bank pulled out of the market narrowed the gains for the Venezuelan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at a midrate of 469.125 bolivars, down from 471.375 Wednesday. Banks quoted spreads ranging from 468.00/469.25 to 469.00/470.25. \par \par \uc2  After \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the morning session by selling dollars at the start of trading, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market again at around 1900 GMT, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At that time, the dollar was quoted around 470.00 bolivars and was showing an upward tendency, traders said. \par \par \uc2  One trader estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  burned between about $30 million and $40 million of foreign reserves to defend the bolivar during trading. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a matter of policy. \par \par \uc2  Although the dollar dropped to about 466.00 bolivars after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Venezuelan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost strength during the last 15 minutes or so of trading, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Strong demand by non-bank clients - including multinational companies - accounted for the bolivar's late-session losses, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Traders speculated that demand for the dollar, as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , could continue Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-05-96 \par \par \uc2  2118GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds5n0481h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
