\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Some See Bolivar Plunging Immediately \b0\par\par\uc2 172 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 1996\par 15:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The bolivar has been fixed at 290 to the dollar since Dec. 11. On the parallel market established by the trading of Venezuelan Brady bonds, the dollar closed Thursday at 465-470 bolivars. The market was closed Friday for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  Before that, the bolivar was frozen at 170 to the dollar since July 1994 after the government imposed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls to stem massive capital flight. \par \par \uc2  Last Monday, President Rafael Caldera announced that Venezuela's 22-month-old \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls would soon be lifted. \par \par \uc2  Traders said opinions were mixed about where the bolivar would trade during the first session. Some said it could bottom out against the dollar, plunging to perhaps 600 bolivars. Others speculated the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the bolivar trading above 500 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'I've heard the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so it doesn't fall below 500,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-04-96 \par \par \uc2  1326GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4m03dv7\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha